Subject: Return a safe value when an AXP2101 register read fails

The charging direction is read from AXP2101 register 0x01. The common I2C
helper previously used ESP_ERROR_CHECK for every read, which aborts firmware
on a transient bus timeout. Log the failure and return zero (neither charging
nor discharging) so battery polling cannot take down the robot.

diff --git a/main/boards/common/i2c_device.cc b/main/boards/common/i2c_device.cc
index 835997d..de8fa4b 100644
--- a/main/boards/common/i2c_device.cc
+++ b/main/boards/common/i2c_device.cc
@@ -29 +29,5 @@ uint8_t I2cDevice::ReadReg(uint8_t reg) {
-    ESP_ERROR_CHECK(i2c_master_transmit_receive(i2c_device_, &reg, 1, buffer, 1, 100));
+    esp_err_t error = i2c_master_transmit_receive(i2c_device_, &reg, 1, buffer, 1, 100);
+    if (error != ESP_OK) {
+        ESP_LOGW(TAG, "I2C register read 0x%02x failed: %s", reg, esp_err_to_name(error));
+        return 0;
+    }
